('node-1-7', 'phase-01-lesson-07-super-method-resolution-order-mro', 'module-2', 7, 'Lesson 2.7: Super(): Method Resolution Order (MRO)', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 1.6', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 1.6 | Subtopics: 4 items', 'Systems project application', 120, 2, 310.0, 350.0, '# Lesson 1.7: Super(): Method Resolution Order (MRO)

- **Status**: `[State: Active | Complete Specification | Core]`
- **Prerequisites**: Lesson 1.6
- **Subtopics**:
  - `1.7.1` Calling parent methods: using super().__init__() to ensure parent initialization runs.
  - `1.7.2` Extending parent behavior: calling super().method() before or after adding child-specific logic.
  - `1.7.3` Method Resolution Order (MRO): the exact order Python uses to search for methods in class hierarchies.
  - `1.7.4` Inspecting class order: using ClassName.mro() to see the inheritance chain.
- **Key Failure Modes & Edge Cases**: Forgetting to call super().__init__() in a subclass, leaving parent attributes uninitialized.
- **Verification & Mastery Check**: Build a SafeTool subclass that calls super().run() and adds automated execution time logging.
- **Project Application**: SchemaAgent: Middleware tool wrapping.', '{"solution.py": "# Phase 1 // Lesson 1.7: Super(): Method Resolution Order (MRO)\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Verification: Build a SafeTool subclass that calls super().run() and adds automated execution time logging.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n"}'::jsonb, '{"lesson": "1.7", "subtopics_count": 4, "verification_criteria": "Build a SafeTool subclass that calls super().run() and adds automated execution time logging.", "subtopics": ["1.7.1 Calling parent methods: using super().__init__() to ensure parent initialization runs.", "1.7.2 Extending parent behavior: calling super().method() before or after adding child-specific logic.", "1.7.3 Method Resolution Order (MRO): the exact order Python uses to search for methods in class hierarchies.", "1.7.4 Inspecting class order: using ClassName.mro() to see the inheritance chain."]}'::jsonb, '["Explain how this implementation prevents: Forgetting to call super().__init__() in a subclass, leaving parent attributes uninitialized.", "How does Super(): Method Resolution Order (MRO) scale under memory and concurrency constraints?", "Defend the architectural tradeoffs of this design in production."]'::jsonb),
('node-1-8', 'phase-01-lesson-08-composition-over-inheritance', 'module-2', 8, 'Lesson 2.8: Composition Over Inheritance', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 1.6', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 1.6 | Subtopics: 4 items', 'Systems project application', 120, 2, 370.0, 400.0, '# Lesson 1.8: Composition Over Inheritance

- **Status**: `[State: Active | Complete Specification | Core]`
- **Prerequisites**: Lesson 1.6
- **Subtopics**:
  - `1.8.1` The architectural golden rule: favor object composition (''has-a'') over class inheritance (''is-a'').
  - `1.8.2` Building systems out of modular parts: assembling an agent from a model, a memory buffer, and tools.
  - `1.8.3` Flexibility benefits: easily swapping components at runtime without changing class inheritance.
  - `1.8.4` Refactoring rigid class hierarchies into clean composed objects.
- **Key Failure Modes & Edge Cases**: Forcing a class to inherit from a parent just to reuse a single helper function.
- **Verification & Mastery Check**: Build an AIAgent class that takes an LLMClient instance and a MemoryBuffer instance via its constructor.
- **Project Application**: SchemaAgent: Composable agent architecture.', '{"solution.py": "# Phase 1 // Lesson 1.8: Composition Over Inheritance\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Verification: Build an AIAgent class that takes an LLMClient instance and a MemoryBuffer instance via its construc\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n"}'::jsonb, '{"lesson": "1.8", "subtopics_count": 4, "verification_criteria": "Build an AIAgent class that takes an LLMClient instance and a MemoryBuffer instance via its constructor.", "subtopics": ["1.8.1 The architectural golden rule: favor object composition (''has-a'') over class inheritance (''is-a'').", "1.8.2 Building systems out of modular parts: assembling an agent from a model, a memory buffer, and tools.", "1.8.3 Flexibility benefits: easily swapping components at runtime without changing class inheritance.", "1.8.4 Refactoring rigid class hierarchies into clean composed objects."]}'::jsonb, '["Explain how this implementation prevents: Forcing a class to inherit from a parent just to reuse a single helper function.", "How does Composition Over Inheritance scale under memory and concurrency constraints?", "Defend the architectural tradeoffs of this design in production."]'::jsonb),
('node-1-9', 'phase-01-lesson-09-dunder-methods-repr-and-str', 'module-2', 9, 'Lesson 2.9: Dunder Methods: __repr__ and __str__', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 1.2', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 1.2 | Subtopics: 4 items', 'Systems project application', 120, 2, 250.0, 450.0, '# Lesson 1.9: Dunder Methods: __repr__ and __str__

- **Status**: `[State: Active | Complete Specification | Core]`
- **Prerequisites**: Lesson 1.2
- **Subtopics**:
  - `1.9.1` Special double-underscore methods: customizing how Python handles your custom objects.
  - `1.9.2` The duality of display: __str__ for human-friendly messages vs __repr__ for unambiguous debugging.
  - `1.9.3` Default object printing: why omitting these methods shows useless <Object at 0x7f...> pointers.
  - `1.9.4` Formatting best practices: making repr(obj) look like valid Python code to recreate the object.
- **Key Failure Modes & Edge Cases**: Failing to implement __repr__, making log files and debugger inspection frustratingly opaque.
- **Verification & Mastery Check**: Implement clean __str__ and __repr__ methods for an AgentAction class showing tool name and arguments.
